{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L150","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":150,"end":151}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":150,"end":151},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:5bcc669f313a8c0198415582ee4ebca0f2dcb8716421a5230fbb9a6c3256ddba","meta":{"text":"1.2: a CASE statement. `operand` is the CASE selector (simple case `CASE x WHEN …`); a searched\ncase (`CASE WHEN cond …`) has no operand. Each branch becomes a `case-branch` condition node."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L169","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":169,"end":169}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":169,"end":169},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:f6118f35d9b93559d54e40521f71ce408e30e7d5d871831b5f98d5592a31f80a","meta":{"text":"An assignment `target := expr;`. 1.2 captures the LHS target so variable provenance is traceable."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L181","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":181,"end":181}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":181,"end":181},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2436ce3a13c4e8f514734121f20131d0dfbc3bfe479c3131a57e1a0708014ee1","meta":{"text":"A procedure/function call statement: `do_work(arg);` / `pkg.do_work(arg);`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L189","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":189,"end":191}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":189,"end":191},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:b6a0078a3a2d95c239ac74d5e0ceaf6a023f30b3b250b5176c8c39eb3293b5ff","meta":{"text":"1.2: a RAISE statement. Covers both `RAISE <name>;` (a named exception) and the re-raise `RAISE;`\n(empty `name`). `RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(code, msg)` is parsed as a raise with `name` set to\n`RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR` and `errorCode`/`errorMessage` split out of the call args."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L204","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":204,"end":205}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":204,"end":205},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:27719e170b9955fa21b850010235f194e7490c23c10c2569c003982f9212aa08","meta":{"text":"A statement we recognize as a statement but don't model further (e.g. NULL;, RETURN). 1.2: an\n`OPEN <cursor>` records the cursor name so an `iterates` edge can link it to the cursor node."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L218","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":218,"end":220}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":218,"end":220},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:8b798de15d6a4e039b1b9e4a2edb1bf2631f4be3cef1eff788973a35ffeba2ae","meta":{"text":"An EXCEPTION block: `EXCEPTION WHEN <cond> THEN ... [WHEN OTHERS THEN ...]`. 1.2: now actually\ninstantiated by the parser (previously defined-but-dead); each handler becomes an\n`exception-handler` node with `whenSelector` + `handles` edges to the guarded statements."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L234","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":234,"end":234}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":234,"end":234},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:28dc5f734e324b28e2d93bf5252c54847a418e6bdb826222a6739d41d07b5056","meta":{"text":"A call site recorded on a unit/decl for cross-file `calls` resolution (extractor → resolver)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L269","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":269,"end":270}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":269,"end":270},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:60be5553b24fa50ca38989918de2861e858b61856aaf087f6ba3a666c2ed6016","meta":{"text":"1.2 (WS-7): a foreign key on a table — the local columns and the referenced table (+ optional\nreferenced columns). `refTable` is as written (may be schema-qualified or bare)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L280","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":280,"end":287}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":280,"end":287},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:3f2ce67bba98181a81bc6af660890e346affeda077aa5fb990eae2b3871f571d","meta":{"text":"A `CREATE [OR REPLACE] TYPE [schema.]name AS OBJECT ( attr type, ... )` definition, or a\ncollection type (`AS TABLE OF <type>` / `AS VARRAY(n) OF <type>`). Object types (e.g. Oracle's\n`T_APPLICANT_CTX_OBJ`) carry a rich attribute list — the migration-relevant \"full DB context\" — so\nthe extractor surfaces them as `symbol` (type:'type') nodes with `meta.attributes`. Collections\nhave an empty attribute list and `meta.collection: { kind, elementType }` instead. A view\n(`CREATE VIEW`) reuses {@link TableDef} with `kind: 'view-ddl'`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L299","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":299,"end":301}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":299,"end":301},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:89576c7e96befe15f591620efacf6ec03028a40aab53694ada9134ea3fead4ff","meta":{"text":"A `CREATE [OR REPLACE] VIEW [schema.]name [( c1, c2, ... )] AS SELECT ...` definition. The view\nbody (the SELECT) is NOT modelled — we capture the name + optional explicit column list so the\nview is an addressable node, not silently dropped."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L311","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":311,"end":311}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":311,"end":311},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:aac41064249a32accee327d31d5e6f5b6d170ebd0be9a2c3fb7db49cf511a39d","meta":{"text":"A top-level construct the parser can produce: an executable unit, a table/view DDL, or a type."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L32","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":32,"end":32}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":32,"end":32},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:5eb0dfa4195829dddff11f2ed8d65a4f4953f4896ad5599d90a226e43935bf16","meta":{"text":"A 1-based inclusive line span."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L38","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":38,"end":38}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":38,"end":38},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ddaa2a4946cd45806d888f7e64dbd8311879dd593ce0525392d31c08a1c11912","meta":{"text":"A top-level PL/SQL unit: a package (spec/body), standalone procedure/function, or anonymous block."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L54","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":54,"end":56}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":54,"end":56},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:708103e39999da24eece43987604e06b1a999e048c7f1c82d0ca36180eb4bd98","meta":{"text":"A declaration inside a unit's declarative part: a nested procedure/function, a local variable,\nor a cursor. 1.2 adds `cursor` (CURSOR c IS SELECT …) with `cursorQuery`, and `variable` carries\n`dataType` so package-level state is recoverable for migration."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L85","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":85,"end":85}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":85,"end":85},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:04864b6d27d25d752e3152c5da74469786b14014db86404fe2a7392b09fca14c","meta":{"text":"A sequence of statements that forms one lexical block. The CFG basic-block unit."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L91","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":91,"end":93}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":91,"end":93},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:df152cf2b91b8d2e8e1fc55e62580841e256ea569e04af552807a200603bd985","meta":{"text":"Discriminated statement union. `sqlKind`/`expr`/`tables`/`columns` drive reads/writes edges.\n1.2 adds `CaseStmt` and `ExceptionBlock` (previously parsed-and-skipped) so guards and handlers\nsurvive into the graph."}}
